From 1c4e248165da1ca21ae77789c010ce7880c3ebb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zac Blanco <zachary.blanco@bytedance.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2025 12:13:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] feat(par_sort): implement merge path sorting for
 OrderBy operator

Introduce ISortBuffer interface and SortBufferMergePath implementation for parallel sorting. Add query config options to enable merge path sorting and control parallelism. Refactor OrderByRowContainer to support spillable containers and improve memory management.

The merge path implementation enables parallel sorting of large datasets by dividing the work across multiple threads. This improves performance for large sorts while maintaining correctness. The new query config options allow controlling the behavior without code changes.

Key changes:
- Add ISortBuffer interface for sort buffer implementations
- Implement SortBufferMergePath using merge path algorithm
- Add query config options for merge path control
- Refactor OrderByRowContainer for better memory management
- Also fixes some concurrency bugs due to poor locking inside of
OrderByRowContainer. The bug was fixed by removing the use of existingPin_ and using an atomic counter instead to add/remove
containers from the LRU list.

- Add tests for new functionality
